WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:03.353
(ethereal vibratory music)

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:04.989
- [Dean] The glass armonica,
really had this effect

00:00:04.989 --> 00:00:07.149
on people who heard it.

00:00:07.149 --> 00:00:09.408
I mean, they were saying
it was the most beautiful

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.308
sound they'd ever heard.

00:00:11.308 --> 00:00:12.388
And there were a lot of beautiful sounds

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:14.484
in the 18th century.

00:00:14.484 --> 00:00:16.418
But you know, there
was something different

00:00:16.418 --> 00:00:19.537
in the sound of the armonica.

00:00:19.537 --> 00:00:22.227
I wanted to give people
that come to Williamsburg

00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:26.394
an experience that they
wouldn't get anywhere else.

00:00:30.341 --> 00:00:32.789
(twangy music)

00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:34.366
- [Chris] I'm Chris Funk.

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:37.028
I'm a musician in a band
called The Decemberists,

00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:39.522
and I'm on a journey looking
for the most surprising

00:00:39.522 --> 00:00:41.644
and extraordinary people in music.

00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:45.568
My next stop takes me to
Williamsburg, Virginia.

00:00:45.568 --> 00:00:48.433
There, I will meet one
of the last true masters

00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:52.350
of an enchanting instrument,
forgotten by time.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:58.388
(ethereal vibratory music)

00:00:58.388 --> 00:00:59.622
I've traveled to Virginia

00:00:59.622 --> 00:01:01.282
and stepped back into history,

00:01:01.282 --> 00:01:03.058
to meet a musician who's perfected

00:01:03.058 --> 00:01:05.641
a rather unusual medium, glass.

00:01:08.058 --> 00:01:09.635
- My name is Dean Shostak,

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:11.091
here in Williamsberg, where I live.

00:01:11.091 --> 00:01:13.060
And I play the glass harmonica,

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.947
but I also play a number of
other glass instruments, too,

00:01:15.947 --> 00:01:18.565
like this Cristal baschet.

00:01:18.565 --> 00:01:20.532
- [Chris] Dean has spent years mastering

00:01:20.532 --> 00:01:22.293
the skills necessary to play this family

00:01:22.293 --> 00:01:24.085
of glass instruments,

00:01:24.085 --> 00:01:26.661
all of which originated
with the glass armonica,

00:01:26.661 --> 00:01:30.411
an instrument with a
very unexpected creator.

00:01:31.653 --> 00:01:33.554
(banjo playing)

00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:37.239
(ethereal vibratory music)

00:01:37.239 --> 00:01:38.741
- [Dean] The glass armonica was invented

00:01:38.741 --> 00:01:41.158
by Benjamin Franklin in 1761.

00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:44.162
He had seen somebody
play on the wine glasses

00:01:44.162 --> 00:01:46.055
in a concert, and he got the idea

00:01:46.055 --> 00:01:47.517
that he could actually use glass

00:01:47.517 --> 00:01:50.029
in an entirely different way.

00:01:50.029 --> 00:01:51.019
You could actually make them rotate

00:01:51.019 --> 00:01:53.698
with a fly wheel you're
working with your foot.

00:01:53.698 --> 00:01:54.531
And with wet fingers,

00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:58.198
you could play it very
much like a keyboard.

00:02:00.348 --> 00:02:02.875
(laughing)

00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:04.480
- Almost had it.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.765
(enchanting music)

00:02:05.765 --> 00:02:07.885
Obviously, you don't tune this instrument.

00:02:07.885 --> 00:02:09.131
- No, that's the one nice thing,

00:02:09.131 --> 00:02:12.236
everybody has to tune to me.

00:02:12.236 --> 00:02:15.462
First thing you need to do is
get your hands really clean.

00:02:15.462 --> 00:02:17.333
And that takes a high calcium content

00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:19.180
in the water, which they happen to have

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.013
here at this theater.

00:02:20.013 --> 00:02:22.110
So, I've got these jugs; I literally

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.655
actually bring the water from the theater

00:02:23.655 --> 00:02:24.815
back to my house,

00:02:24.815 --> 00:02:28.591
to have the same water to
play with all the time.

00:02:28.591 --> 00:02:29.848
The skin absorbs moisture,

00:02:29.848 --> 00:02:31.368
and so you really want your hands

00:02:31.368 --> 00:02:33.856
to start wrinkling up a little bit, too.

00:02:33.856 --> 00:02:35.624
The condition of the skin on your fingers

00:02:35.624 --> 00:02:38.958
is really what produces the sounds.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:39.883
(ethereal vibratory music)

00:02:39.883 --> 00:02:41.527
- [Chris] And those
mesmerizing sounds produced

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.232
by skin on glass are not limited

00:02:43.232 --> 00:02:46.117
to the glass armonica
or the Cristal baschet.

00:02:46.117 --> 00:02:50.166
The technique has led to some
truly bizarre instruments.

00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:52.131
(trumpeting)

00:02:52.131 --> 00:02:53.305
Wow.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:55.722
(trumpeting)

00:03:02.109 --> 00:03:03.551
(hornlike vibrating)

00:03:03.551 --> 00:03:05.199
- [Dean] I've heard the
argument made that, you know,

00:03:05.199 --> 00:03:08.875
we've gone as far as we can
with acoustic instruments.

00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:10.470
(trumpeting)

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:11.398
If you think about glass music

00:03:11.398 --> 00:03:14.261
as a still unexplored musical frontier,

00:03:14.261 --> 00:03:15.094
it's pretty exciting to think

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.086
what instruments we could try in glass.

00:03:17.086 --> 00:03:19.216
You know, but we don't know until
we make these instruments

00:03:19.216 --> 00:03:21.466
what they're gonna be like.

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:26.334
(ethereal vibratory music)

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.678
I think we should know
about the glass armonica,

00:03:27.678 --> 00:03:30.043
because it's truly the
first American instrument,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:34.210
you know, aside from the Native American
instruments already here.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:38.193
I absolutely had to
teach myself how to play.

00:03:38.193 --> 00:03:40.652
My only sources were
reading what Franklin wrote

00:03:40.652 --> 00:03:43.669
and these other guys back in the time.

00:03:43.669 --> 00:03:45.461
It is new every day.

00:03:45.461 --> 00:03:46.893
Every time I sit down
and play the armonica,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.629
it is a fresh experience

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:50.841
and a challenge each time.

00:03:50.841 --> 00:03:54.424
(ethereal vibratory music)

